ilities\nGroups and centres\nBecome a research student\nWork with us\nResearch Connect\nPartner with UC\nFind an expert\nResources\nFacilities and field stations\nResearch publications\nContact Research & Innovation\nkeyboard_arrow_right\nRongo o te W\u0101\nNews and Events\nkeyboard_arrow_left\nBack\nclose\nClose\nNews and Events\nRongo o te W\u0101\nkeyboard_arrow_right\nNews and Events overview\nLatest News\nNews\nStudent notices\nEvents\nEvents\nRegular events and celebrations\nFuture students\nCurrent students\nInternational\nPostgraduates\nAlumni\nUC Online\nStaff\nHome\nkeyboard_arrow_right\nStudy\nkeyboard_arrow_right\nAcademic study options\nkeyboard_arrow_right\nSubjects\nkeyboard_arrow_right\nmore_horiz\nUndergraduate subject\nData Science\n15 October 2026\nDevelop the skills to meet global demand for data science university graduates.\nHOW TO APPLY\nApply for a qualification\nCheck your eligibility\nOverview\nData Science\nData Science is an emerging field that combines Computer Science, Mathematics, and Statistics with other disciplines. Studying Data Science at the University of Canterbury, you will learn to understand and analyse data, and communicate your findings for the best possible decision-making.\nWhat will my study involve?\nkeyboard_arrow_down\nData Science\nInvestigate the many sources and applications of data in healthcare, business, transport, and economics.\nGet hands-on in the field in connection with UC\u2019s various research centres.\nProject work in your final year where you will be applying data science in the workplace.\nCourses\nkeyboard_arrow_down\nData Science\nSee all Data Science courses\nBachelor of Data Science\nSee the Bachelor of Data Science for the compulsory Data Science courses in the degree.\nAs well as the core courses, you will also study towards one of the following majors:\nData Science (see below)\nBioinformatics\nBusiness Analytics\nPopulation Health Data Science\nSpatial Data Science\nData Science major\nComplete the compulsory courses for the Bachelor of Data Science, along with the following major courses:\n100-level\nAny 100-level course at UC\n200-level\nCOSC265 Relational Database Systems\nOne course from STAT211\u2013299\n300-level\nCOSC367 Artificial Intelligence\nDATA309 Data Science Capstone Project\nSTAT315 Multivariate Statistical Methods\nIn addition to the major requirements above, and the compulsory Bachelor of Data Science courses, any additional electives to achieve a total of 360 points should be selected from:\nAny 200-level course at UC\n300-level COSC courses\n300-level DATA courses\n300-level MATH courses\n300-level SENG courses\n300-level STAT courses\nCareer opportunities\nkeyboard_arrow_down\nData Science\nWith such a wide range of industry applications, Data Science is one of the most essential and employable skills of the 21st century.\nCareer pathways could include:\ndata scientist\nbusiness and technology analyst\ndata visualisation consultant\ninsights consultant.\nFind out more about what you can do with a degree in Data Science.\nBrochures\nUndergraduate Prospectus 2027\nWhakatairanga \u0100konga\nDownload\n(application/pdf,\n2 MB)\ndownload\nDownload\nInternational Prospectus 2027\nDownload\n(application/pdf,\n8 MB)\ndownload\nDownload\nQualifications\nDiploma in Science\nBachelor of Data Science\nContact us\nContact Science\nScholarships\nScholarships\nRelated subjects\nChoose an area that you are interested in and learn how UC\u2019s range of study options can let you study what you want to.\nSoftware Engineering\n21 October 2026\nDevelop software engineering skills through foundational courses and practical work.\nSoftware Engineering\nDevelop software engineering skills through foundational courses and practical work.\nSoftware Engineering\nPressing this button will open your email client.\nPressing this button will start a call.\nSoftware Engineering\nDevelop software engineering skills through foundational courses and practical work.\